Report tail -c errors on seekable files in the exit status.
For -c on a seekable file tail copies the bytes with bb_copyfd_size and
ignored its result, so a read error or a write error (for example to a
full disk) was printed but tail still exited 0.

Set the failure exit status when the copy fails, as tail_read does for
other read errors.

---
 coreutils/tail.c |    3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/coreutils/tail.c
+++ b/coreutils/tail.c
@@ -234,7 +234,8 @@
 					if (current < 0)
 						current = 0;
 					xlseek(fd, current, SEEK_SET);
-					bb_copyfd_size(fd, STDOUT_FILENO, count);
+					if (bb_copyfd_size(fd, STDOUT_FILENO, count) < 0)
+						G.exitcode = EXIT_FAILURE;
 					continue;
 				}
 #if 1 /* This is technically incorrect for *LONG* strings, but very useful */
